The '''Ghrazi rapier''' is a one-handed [[stab weapon]] obtainable as a rare drop from the [[Theatre of Blood]]. It requires level 80 [[Attack]] to wield. It provides the highest strength and stab bonus out of any weapon for its [[attack speed]]. This makes the rapier tied with the [[blade of Saeldor]] and the [[Inquisitor's mace]] for the [[melee]] weapon with the highest damage output for general use, although it is outperformed by the [[Osmumten's fang]] against high defence monsters and [[Scythe of Vitur]] against large monsters.

The Ghrazi tribe was the most vicious [[vampyre]] tribe on [[Vampyrium]]. This rapier was once wielded by a fearsome Ghrazi warlord who was slain in battle by [[Verzik Vitur]]'s [[Sugadinti Vitur|father]], who gave it to Verzik.{{CiteNews|url=http://services.runescape.com/m=news/the-theatre-of-blood?oldschool=1|title=The Theatre of Blood|newsdate=7 June 2018|quote=Of all Vampyriums tribes, none were more vicious than the Ghrazi. These vampyres took pride in their combat abilities and would regularly bait their prey into battle so that they could test their prowess. The rapier in Lady Verzik's vault was once wielded by a fearsome Ghrazi warlord. It was given to her by her father who came to possess it after the warlord challenged him to a battle, one that he did not survive to tell the tale.}}

The rapier can be combined with a [[holy ornament kit]] to make a [[Saradomin]]-themed [[holy Ghrazi rapier]]. This cosmetic upgrade won't change the stats in any way, but it will make the rapier count as a Saradomin item in the [[God Wars Dungeon]].

